PART 2 �� one-variable reduction (SP-F-LOOPALG sec.3): reproduce 5.44 -> 8.8e14
==============================================================================
  (star_1): c1 f'' = c2 g^2 N f^2 / R^3,  f = e^{-sigma R^2}, sigma=1, c1/c2=1
  => LHS/RHS = (4R^2-2) R^3 e^{+sigma R^2}   (grows like e^{+sigma R^2} R^5)
    R=1:  LHS/RHS =       5.4366
    R=2:  LHS/RHS =         6115
    R=3:  LHS/RHS =   7.4386e+06
    R=5:  LHS/RHS =   8.8206e+14
  one-variable residual ratio R=1 -> R=5:  1.622e+14
  (SP-F-LOOPALG quotes 5.44 -> 8.8e14, i.e. 1.62e+14; agreement: rel.diff 2.34e-03)

