PART 3 �� two-variable residual (this work): rho = LHS/RHS on C_R,theta
==============================================================================
  local loop derivative: dW/dsigma_{mu nu}(x) = -(sigma/2) eps_{mu nu} chi_S(x) W
  => d_mu(...) = (sigma/2) W t_nu delta_C      [boundary term; NOT identically 0]
  RHS: oint dy_nu delta^4(x-y) G(y) = g^2 N G(R,theta) t_nu delta_C
  => rho(R,theta) = (sigma/2) W / (g^2 N G) = sigma/(2 g^2 N)  [W=G by additivity]
    R=1: rho = 0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000
    R=2: rho = 0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000
    R=3: rho = 0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000
    R=5: rho = 0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000  0.500000000000
  spread over (R,theta): max=0.500000000000 min=0.500000000000 -> ratio = 1.000000000000
  two-variable residual ratio R=1 -> R=5 : 1.000000000000

  sigma condition: rho == 1  <=>  sigma = 2 g^2 N   (R- and theta-independent)
    e.g. g^2 N=1 -> sigma = 2;  g^2 N=0.5 -> sigma = 1

