PART 4 �� robustness: subleading prefactors in G do not resurrect an R-power
==============================================================================
  G <- G(1+0.1/R):  rho(1)=0.454545  rho(5)=0.490196  ratio=1.078431   (still O(1))
  G <- G(1+1.0/R):  rho(1)=0.250000  rho(5)=0.416667  ratio=1.666667   (still O(1))

==============================================================================
PART 5 �� DIMENSION TABLE (machine-checked, exponents of L only)
==============================================================================
  [W]=L^0  [A]=L^2  [sigma]=L^-2  [g^2N]=L^0   (4D: g dimensionless)
  [LHS] = [d_mu][d/dsigma] = L^{-3};  [RHS] = [g^2N][dy][delta^4] = L^{-3}   -> MATCH
  literal 'sigma = 2 g^2 N'      : L^-2 vs L^0   -> off by L^{-2}  (DIMENSIONALLY WRONG)
  contact-term form 'sigma = 2 g^2 N mu^2': L^-2 vs L^-2   -> MATCH
  where mu enters: oint dy_nu delta^4(x-y) |_{x=y on C} = t_nu * delta^3_perp(0)
  i.e. the coincidence/contact term (C3-COEFF sec.2: prescription is an extra input).
  Lattice units a=1:  mu = 1/a  ->  sigma a^2 = 2 g^2 N  (dimensionless, OK).

