VERDICT
==============================================================================
  one-variable  : 5.44 -> 8.8e14   (ratio 1.62e+14, growth e^{+sigma R^2}R^5)
  two-variable  : 0.500 -> 0.500   (ratio 1.000000000000)
  residual: identically 0 once sigma = 2 g^2 N mu^2 is imposed; otherwise the
  residual is the CONSTANT sigma/(2 g^2 N mu^2) -- no R-power, no theta-mismatch.
  => area law IS a solution of (star) on the planar two-variable sector  [(a) / [C]]
  price: the equation fixes only sigma/mu^2, not sigma itself (contact scale mu is
  an extra input) -> consistency, not a derivation of the string tension.
